// Method:
//   1. Fetch and normalize the Hipparcos main catalog.
//   2. Prefilter stars by V magnitude <= 4.50 and ecliptic-latitude band
//      within ±12.0° of the north precession circle (~66.56°).
//   3. Scan epochs -4000 to 14000 in 10-year steps with Astropy.
//   4. Keep one best-fit row per HIP at its minimum separation from the north celestial pole.
// Data rows use:
//   [year, ra_j2000_deg, dec_j2000_deg, hip, name, min_sep_deg, magnitude]
// Summary:
//   catalog rows cached: 117955
//   stars scanned after prefilter: 66
//   emitted results with min_sep_deg <= 7.00: 30

